@startuml contribution2_dual_execution_modes
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 220
skinparam ranksep 28
skinparam nodesep 18
top to bottom direction

title Dual execution modes — **WebSocket peer** and **embodied entity**

legend top left
  How to read
  - Obs: game to Python (kind: observation)
  - Act: Python to game (kind: action)
  - hello: role client or role server
  - Read each scenario **top to bottom** (return arrows show Act coming back).
endlegend


' ─── Scenario A (stacked vertically) ─────────────────────────
rectangle "**A. PLAYER** — AI drives the **local player**" as RA #E3F2FD {

  component "Minecraft\n**Client**" as A_MC
  component "ClientBridgeHooks\n(build & send obs)" as A_CBH
  component "ForgeWebSocketClient\n**hello → role=client**" as A_FWS
  component "**Python bridge**" as A_PY
  component "**LocalPlayer**\n(client-side input)" as A_LP

  A_MC -down-> A_CBH : sample **Obs**\n(player, level, rays, …)
  A_CBH -down-> A_FWS : **Obs** JSON
  A_FWS -down-> A_PY : WebSocket **Obs**
  A_PY -up-> A_FWS : WebSocket **Act**
  A_FWS -down-> A_LP : **Act**\n(execute on client)
  A_LP -up-> A_MC : affects **world**\n(vanilla replication in MP)
}

note bottom of RA
  **ControlMode.PLAYER** — typical for single-player / integrated server
  and client-driven control in multiplayer.
end note


' ─── Scenario B (A-style boxes + Forge play networking vs WebSocket) ──
rectangle "**B. SERVER_BOT** — AI drives **server fake player**" as RB #E8F5E9 {

  component "Minecraft\n**Dedicated server**" as B_MC
  component "FakeBotManager\n(build & send obs)" as B_FBM
  component "ServerBridgeWebSocketClient\n**hello → role=server**" as B_SWS
  component "**Python bridge**" as B_PY
  component "**FakePlayer**\n(authoritative server bot)" as B_BOT
  component "Forge **BotNet**\n(play channel, custom packets)" as B_NET

  B_MC -down-> B_FBM : sample **Obs**\n(world, ticks, …)
  B_BOT -up-> B_FBM : sample **Obs**\n(bot pose, inv, …)
  B_FBM -down-> B_SWS : **Obs** JSON
  B_SWS -down-> B_PY : WebSocket **Obs**
  B_PY -up-> B_SWS : WebSocket **Act**
  B_SWS -up-> B_FBM : **Act**
  B_FBM -down-> B_BOT : **Act**\n(server applies)
  B_BOT -up-> B_MC : **world state**\n(authoritative)

  B_FBM ..> B_NET : **S2C** bot state\n(S2CBotStatePacket)
  B_NET -up-> B_MC : **PLAY_TO_CLIENT**\n(remote game clients)
  B_NET ..> B_SWS : **C2S** from clients\n→ sendConfigUpdate\n(runtime / control_mode)
}

note bottom of RB
  **ControlMode.SERVER_BOT** — the **game client** does not own the WebSocket;
  **ServerBotHooks** (Forge lifecycle) runs in this JVM and wires the mod.
  **BotNet** is the normal **Minecraft play** channel (S2C / C2S), separate from the **WebSocket** to Python.
end note

RA -[hidden]down- RB

note bottom of B_PY
  **One bridge port → one active game peer.**
  Use **A** (client WebSocket) **xor** **B** (server WebSocket),
  not two connections to the same policy loop.
end note

@enduml
